## Resolution

- Optional independent gate/up/down output biases work in all five compact/factored execution, backward and SGD paths. Mixed absent/present biases retain exactly their declared parameters; gradients accumulate, and source weights stay unchanged on a failed step.
- Pruning selects gate/up biases and keeps the down bias; spline controls preserve them; SVD adds each output bias after L*R. Affine score method IDs /1 state the augmented-row/calibration energy heuristic.
- Schema 4 requires a semantic descriptor. Unsupported block kinds, source activations, dtype/layout, state, parameter sharing and requested devices are refused without fallback. Earlier schemas are named in the refusal before reading new required fields; no compatibility reader was added.
- On 52773a8e, after staging cac5b40e, **31 host tests**, both portable release rlibs and **12 external forward/backward/SGD/exact-round-trip cases** passed on the NRL branch. No build or test ran on fast-test.
- Every trainable bias and factor has an independent finite-difference check. The fixture separately marks five unmodified QSL cases, five PyTorch affine extensions and two rectangular affine extensions. The original QSL converter itself still refuses biases.
- Fixture regeneration was byte-identical (SHA-256 85cd6f82b729c0843a54717a4e97fd1716239192008e0d073026337ebfbb211a); the maximum recorded reference error is 5.684341886080802e-14. Evidence: `nrl/reports/affine-f64-2026-10-26.json` and `affine-check-2026-10-26.txt`.
- This completes the five-representation numerical path for the stated gated SiLU CPU f64 profile, including affine projection behaviour. It does not complete full-model/graph contracts, model import, another operator family, real-model benefit or native execution. Parent 900 and T04 onward remain open.
